  "label": "User projected onto the abusive accusation scene",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the abusive accusation scene, which is composed of the visual material of Hillary Clinton and the textual material accusing her of finding humor in violent acts. The meme's structure implies the user is identifying with the moral outrage or the accusatory stance, projecting their own judgment or anger onto the scene. There are no explicit deictic pronouns like 'me' or 'you' in the text, but the accusatory tone and the framing of the scene create an implicit projection where the user sees themselves as the moral arbiter or victim of the situation described. The user is projected onto the scene as the one who is outraged by the alleged behavior, thereby internalizing the meme's moral framework.",
